packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-1--- Migration 208: 03-technical Gate-4 corrective — BOM version state machine: forbid
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-2--- technical_approved -> in_review (in-place re-open of an immutable approved version).
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-3--- PRD: docs/prd/03-TECHNICAL-PRD.md §0, §5.1A, §7.1, §7.4, §7.6. Task T-073.
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-4---
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql:5:-- ROOT CAUSE: migration 168 (168-bom-version-state-machine-clone-on-write.sql:79) allows
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-6---   when 'technical_approved' then new.status in ('in_review', 'active', 'superseded', 'archived')
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-7--- Re-opening an approved (immutable) version in place by moving it back to 'in_review' violates
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql:8:-- the clone-on-write invariant: once a version reaches technical_approved it must only terminalize
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-9--- (active/superseded/archived), never re-enter a working/review state. Any post-approval change
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql:10:-- must create a NEW draft version via the clone-on-write helper public.bom_request_version_edit()
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-11--- (168 §2), which inserts a fresh in_review version that supersedes the approved one — the
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-12--- approved row is never mutated.
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-13---
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-14--- WHY THIS IS THE CLEAN INVARIANT FIX (verified, fix APPLIED — not skipped):
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-15---   * The 090 content-lock trigger (bom_headers_reject_approved_content_update, 090:115-148)
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-16---     already blocks all CONTENT-field changes on technical_approved/active rows, so the only
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-17---     legal UPDATE on those rows is the lifecycle transition itself. Removing in_review from the
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-18---     allowed set therefore closes the LAST in-place re-open path without affecting content edits.
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql:19:--   * The canonical re-review flow is clone-on-write (a NEW in_review version), not reopening the
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-20---     approved row. The 168 clone helper, the apps/web/packages services, and the T-073 test suite
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-21---     all exercise that path; NOTHING in the codebase drives technical_approved -> in_review in
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-22---     place, and no test asserts that transition is allowed. So it is NOT load-bearing.
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-23---
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-24--- This `create or replace`s the transition guard with the IDENTICAL body except that in_review is
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-25--- removed from technical_approved's allowed set (active/superseded/archived retained). The trigger
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-26--- itself is unchanged (still wired by 168); replacing the function is sufficient. Idempotent.
packages/db/migrations/208-bom-state-machine-no-reopen-technical-approved.sql-27--- Wave0 lock: org_id business scope; the guard is org-agnostic (operates on status only).
--
